        <scopecontent id="aspace_f666a2664c32cf945b4ca663c7468ae7">
          <head>Scope and Contents</head>
          <p>Series VII includes non-commercial and commercially released audiovisual material containing performances, interviews, studio recordings, and other recordings documenting the work of Henri Chopin and other musicians and poets. The Sound Recordings subseries includes sound recordings by Chopin and others across several formats. Most of the reel-to-reel audiotapes by Chopin were likely used in his performances. The Video Recordings subseries includes VHS, BetacamSP, and DVD recordings of Chopin and his contemporaries. The Other Audiovisual Material subseries contains digital audiotapes and computer disks by Chopin and various sound recording equipment owned by Chopin, including three reel-to-reel tape recorders, two microphones, and an audiotape cutter and scissors.</p>
        </scopecontent>
        <arrangement id="aspace_eb41c295fecde0ab26107dbeba76ae7f">
          <head>Arrangement</head>
          <p>Organized into three subseries: Sound Recordings, Video Recordings, and Other Audiovisual Material.</p>
        </arrangement>
        <accessrestrict id="aspace_33f677634bc0f49f396f095375a54b04">
          <head>Conditions Governing Access</head>
          <p>Boxes 37-53 and 72 (sound recordings): Restricted fragile material. Reference copies may be requested. Consult Access Services for further information.</p>
          <p>Box 81 (computer disks): ‡a Restricted Fragile Material. Reference copies of electronic files may be requested. Consult Access Services for further information.</p>
          <p>Boxes 54-71 and 73-80 (sound and video) Restricted fragile material. Reference copies may be requested. Consult Access Services for further information.</p>
        </accessrestrict>
